WEBVTT

00:03:14.970 --> 00:03:16.937
<i>Kristin: hey, meredith, it's kristin.</i>

00:03:16.970 --> 00:03:19.137
<i>You have to tell me
what happened last night.</i>

00:03:19.170 --> 00:03:20.137
<i>Call me.</i>

00:03:21.337 --> 00:03:23.471
<i>Brad: hey, meredith. Brad calling.</i>

00:03:23.504 --> 00:03:26.304
<i>Listen, do you want to hook up later?</i>

00:03:26.337 --> 00:03:29.671
<i>Well, i'll talk to you
then. Give me a call. Thanks.</i>

00:03:34.271 --> 00:03:36.738
<i>Brock: hey, meredith, what's
going on? This is brock.</i>

00:03:36.770 --> 00:03:39.571
<i>I just wanted to let you know
the gang is gonna get together.</i>

00:03:39.604 --> 00:03:41.404
<i>We're gonna go to the garage.</i>

00:03:41.437 --> 00:03:43.437
<i>We're gonna have some
beers and some shots.</i>

00:04:13.970 --> 00:04:16.937
All right, dean, this is the place.

00:04:16.970 --> 00:04:18.937
I've got to say dad and me did just fine

00:04:18.970 --> 00:04:21.304
Without these stupid costumes.

00:04:21.337 --> 00:04:24.638
I feel like a
high-School-Drama dork.

00:04:26.504 --> 00:04:28.471
What was that play that you did?

00:04:28.504 --> 00:04:30.304
What was it
-- "Our town"?

00:04:30.337 --> 00:04:31.970
Yeah, you were good. It was cute.

00:04:32.004 --> 00:04:33.803
Look, you want to pull this off or not?

00:04:33.837 --> 00:04:36.337
I'm just saying these outfits
cost hard-Earned money.

00:04:36.371 --> 00:04:37.437
Whose?

00:04:37.471 --> 00:04:40.803
Ours. You think
credit-Card fraud is easy?

00:04:43.070 --> 00:04:45.037
Thanks for letting us look around.

00:04:45.070 --> 00:04:48.571
The police said they were
done with the place, so...

00:04:59.204 --> 00:05:01.337
You guys said you were
with the alarm company?

00:05:01.371 --> 00:05:02.704
That's right.

00:05:02.738 --> 00:05:04.004
Well, no offense,

00:05:04.037 --> 00:05:07.170
But your alarm is about as
useful as boobs on a man.

00:05:07.204 --> 00:05:09.170
Well, that's
why we're here --

00:05:09.204 --> 00:05:12.537
To see what went wrong, to
stop it from happening again.

00:05:14.571 --> 00:05:16.371
Now, ma'am, you found the body?

00:05:16.404 --> 00:05:17.537
Yeah.

00:05:17.571 --> 00:05:18.870
Right after it happened?

00:05:18.903 --> 00:05:20.204
No, a few days later.

00:05:20.237 --> 00:05:22.870
Meredith's work called.
She hadn't showed up.

00:05:22.903 --> 00:05:24.970
I knocked on her door.

00:05:25.004 --> 00:05:27.937
That's when i noticed... the smell.

00:05:27.970 --> 00:05:31.404
Any windows open? Any sign of break-In?

00:05:31.437 --> 00:05:32.870
Windows were locked.
Front door was bolted.

00:05:32.903 --> 00:05:35.271
Chain was on the door. We
had to cut it to get in.

00:05:35.304 --> 00:05:36.604
And the alarm was still on?

00:05:36.638 --> 00:05:39.604
Like i said. Bang-Up job
your company is doing.

00:05:39.638 --> 00:05:41.704
Did you see any overturned furniture,

00:05:41.738 --> 00:05:43.371
Broken glass, signs of struggle?

00:05:43.404 --> 00:05:46.337
Everything was in perfect condition...

00:05:46.371 --> 00:05:48.271
Except meredith.

00:05:48.304 --> 00:05:51.437
Well, what condition was meredith in?

00:05:51.471 --> 00:05:54.837
Meredith was all over, in pieces.

00:05:54.870 --> 00:05:57.704
The guy who killed her
must have been a whack job.

00:05:57.738 --> 00:06:00.304
But i tell you, if i
didn't know any better,

00:06:00.337 --> 00:06:02.537
I'd have said a wild animal did it.

00:06:05.571 --> 00:06:08.170
Ma'am, you mind if we take some time,

00:06:08.204 --> 00:06:10.271
Give this place a once-Over?

00:06:10.304 --> 00:06:13.704
Go right ahead. Knock yourself out.

00:06:19.104 --> 00:06:21.237
So the killer walks in
and out of the apartment --

00:06:21.271 --> 00:06:22.738
No weapons, no prints, nothing.

00:06:22.770 --> 00:06:25.070
I'm telling you, the
minute i found that article,

00:06:25.104 --> 00:06:26.738
I knew this was our kind of gig.

00:06:26.770 --> 00:06:28.271
I think i agree with you.

00:06:28.304 --> 00:06:30.770
So, you talked to the cops?

00:06:30.803 --> 00:06:34.304
Uh, yeah, i
spoke to amy --

00:06:34.337 --> 00:06:38.304
A, uh, charming, perky
officer of the law.

00:06:38.337 --> 00:06:39.638
What did you find out?

00:06:39.671 --> 00:06:42.638
Well, she's a sagittarius.
She loves tequila.

00:06:42.671 --> 00:06:44.837
I mean...whew.

00:06:44.870 --> 00:06:47.004
Oh, and she's got this
little tattoo. Dean!

00:06:47.037 --> 00:06:48.170
What? Yeah.

00:06:48.204 --> 00:06:50.004
Nothing we don't already know,

00:06:50.037 --> 00:06:53.304
Except for one thing they're
keeping out of the papers.

00:06:53.337 --> 00:06:54.770
Meredith's heart was missing.

00:06:56.604 --> 00:06:57.738
Her heart?

00:06:57.770 --> 00:07:00.237
Yeah, her heart.

00:07:00.271 --> 00:07:02.070
So, what do you think did it to her?

00:07:02.104 --> 00:07:04.471
The landlady said it looked
like an animal attack.

00:07:04.504 --> 00:07:07.371
Maybe it was. Werewolf?

00:07:07.404 --> 00:07:09.271
Not a werewolf. The
lunar cycle's not right.

00:07:09.304 --> 00:07:10.337
If it was a creature,

00:07:10.371 --> 00:07:12.137
It would've left some kind of trace.

00:07:12.170 --> 00:07:15.803
It was probably a spirit.

00:07:15.837 --> 00:07:17.937
Hmm.

00:07:17.970 --> 00:07:21.471
See if you can find
any masking tape around.

00:07:44.070 --> 00:07:46.371
Ever see that symbol before?

00:07:46.404 --> 00:07:48.837
Never.

00:07:48.870 --> 00:07:50.837
Me, neither.

00:08:24.204 --> 00:08:26.504
I talked to the bartender.

00:08:26.537 --> 00:08:28.937
Did you get anything...
besides her number?

00:08:28.970 --> 00:08:32.803
Dude, i'm a professional.
I'm offended that...

00:08:34.437 --> 00:08:37.037
All right.

00:08:37.070 --> 00:08:39.237
You mind doing a little bit of thinking

00:08:39.271 --> 00:08:41.070
With your upstairs brain, dean?

00:08:41.104 --> 00:08:42.803
Hmm? There's nothing to find out.

00:08:42.837 --> 00:08:44.837
Meredith worked here. She waited tables.

00:08:44.870 --> 00:08:47.371
Everyone here is her friend.
Everyone says she's normal.

00:08:47.404 --> 00:08:49.704
She didn't do or say anything
weird before she died.

00:08:49.738 --> 00:08:51.970
What about that symbol?
Did you find anything?

00:08:52.004 --> 00:08:53.371
Nope. Nothing.

00:08:53.404 --> 00:08:55.870
It wasn't in dad's journal
or in any of the usual books.

00:08:55.903 --> 00:08:58.638
I just have to dig a
little deeper, i guess.

00:08:58.671 --> 00:09:02.037
There was a first victim,
right, before meredith?

00:09:02.070 --> 00:09:04.037
Right, yeah. His name was, uh...

00:09:04.070 --> 00:09:06.070
His name was ben swardstrom.

00:09:06.104 --> 00:09:08.738
Last month he was found
mutilated in his town house.

00:09:08.770 --> 00:09:11.803
Same deal. The door was
locked. The alarm was on.

00:09:11.837 --> 00:09:13.738
Is there any connection between them?

00:09:13.770 --> 00:09:15.070
Nothing i could tell.

00:09:15.104 --> 00:09:17.104
Ben was a banker.
Meredith was a waitress.

00:09:17.137 --> 00:09:19.204
They never met, never
knew anyone in common.

00:09:19.237 --> 00:09:21.571
They were practically
from different worlds.

00:09:21.604 --> 00:09:23.404
So the only successful
intel we've scored

00:09:23.437 --> 00:09:26.104
Is the bartender's phone number.

00:09:27.204 --> 00:09:29.404
What?

00:09:32.437 --> 00:09:33.604
Sam?

00:09:41.970 --> 00:09:43.104
Meg.

00:09:43.137 --> 00:09:44.704
Sam!

00:09:48.970 --> 00:09:53.170
Sam, is that you? Oh, my gosh!

00:09:54.970 --> 00:09:57.970
What are you doing here?

00:09:58.003 --> 00:09:59.937
I'm just in town
-- Visiting friends.

00:10:01.903 --> 00:10:03.037
Where are they?

00:10:03.070 --> 00:10:05.371
Well, they're not here right now,

00:10:05.404 --> 00:10:06.970
But what about you, meg?

00:10:07.003 --> 00:10:08.838
I thought you were going to california.

00:10:08.870 --> 00:10:10.170
Oh, i did.

00:10:10.204 --> 00:10:12.371
I came. I saw. I conquered.

00:10:12.404 --> 00:10:14.903
Oh, and i met
what's his name --

00:10:14.937 --> 00:10:17.404
Something michael
murray -- At a bar.

00:10:17.437 --> 00:10:18.571
Who?

00:10:18.604 --> 00:10:19.838
It doesn't matter.

00:10:19.870 --> 00:10:22.237
Anyway, the whole scene got old,

00:10:22.270 --> 00:10:24.537
So i'm living here for a while.

00:10:25.771 --> 00:10:27.070
You're from chicago?

00:10:27.104 --> 00:10:30.070
No, massachusetts
-- Andover.

00:10:30.104 --> 00:10:31.637
Gosh, sam,

00:10:31.671 --> 00:10:33.838
What are the odds we'd
run into each other?

00:10:33.870 --> 00:10:35.838
I know. I thought i'd
never see you again.

00:10:35.870 --> 00:10:38.104
Well, i'm glad you were wrong.

00:10:41.537 --> 00:10:43.537
Dude, cover your mouth.

00:10:43.571 --> 00:10:46.437
Yeah, i'm sorry, meg.

00:10:46.471 --> 00:10:49.671
This is, um -- This
is my brother, dean.

00:10:51.704 --> 00:10:52.903
This is dean?

00:10:52.937 --> 00:10:54.704
Yeah. So you've heard of me?

00:10:54.738 --> 00:10:56.537
Oh, yeah, i've heard of you.

00:10:56.571 --> 00:11:00.337
Nice -- The way you treat
your brother like luggage.

00:11:00.371 --> 00:11:01.671
Sorry?

00:11:01.704 --> 00:11:04.270
Why don't you let him
do what he wants to do?

00:11:04.304 --> 00:11:06.704
Stop dragging him
over god's green earth.

00:11:06.738 --> 00:11:08.903
Meg...it's all right.

00:11:11.237 --> 00:11:14.371
Okay. Awkward.

00:11:14.404 --> 00:11:17.437
I'm gonna get a drink now.

00:11:22.003 --> 00:11:23.304
Sam, i'm sorry.

00:11:23.337 --> 00:11:28.003
It's just, the way you
told me he treats you,

00:11:28.037 --> 00:11:29.870
If it were me, i'd kill him.

00:11:29.903 --> 00:11:31.404
It's all right. He means well.

00:11:31.437 --> 00:11:34.037
We should hook up while you're in town.

00:11:34.070 --> 00:11:35.204
Yeah.

00:11:35.237 --> 00:11:37.237
I could show you a hell of a time.

00:11:37.270 --> 00:11:38.537
That sounds great.

00:11:38.571 --> 00:11:40.537
Why don't you give me your number?

00:11:40.571 --> 00:11:43.870

312-555-0143.

00:11:43.903 --> 00:11:45.738
You know what? I never
got your last name.

00:11:45.771 --> 00:11:47.371
Masters. Masters?

00:11:47.404 --> 00:11:48.604
So you better call.

00:11:48.637 --> 00:11:50.604
Scout's honor.

00:11:50.637 --> 00:11:54.637
I hope to see you around, sam.

00:12:04.137 --> 00:12:05.437
Who the hell we he?

00:12:05.471 --> 00:12:07.437
I don't really know.
I only met her once.

00:12:07.471 --> 00:12:09.771
Meeting up with her again?

00:12:09.804 --> 00:12:13.104
I don't know, man. It's weird.

00:12:13.137 --> 00:12:15.771
What was she saying --
I treat you like luggage?

00:12:15.804 --> 00:12:17.771
Were you bitching
about me to some chick?

00:12:17.804 --> 00:12:19.104
Look, i'm sorry, dean.

00:12:19.137 --> 00:12:20.604
It was when we had that huge fight

00:12:20.637 --> 00:12:22.637
When i was in the bus stop in indiana.

00:12:22.671 --> 00:12:24.637
Is there any truth to what she's saying?

00:12:24.671 --> 00:12:26.504
Am i keeping you against your will, sam?

00:12:26.537 --> 00:12:28.437
No, of course not.
Now, would you listen?

00:12:28.471 --> 00:12:30.437
What?!

00:12:30.471 --> 00:12:32.937
I think there's something
strange going on here, dean.

00:12:32.970 --> 00:12:34.571
Tell me about it. She
wasn't even into me.

00:12:34.604 --> 00:12:37.137
No, man, i mean, like
our kind of strange.

00:12:37.170 --> 00:12:39.137
Maybe even a lead. Why do you say that?

00:12:39.170 --> 00:12:41.937
I met meg weeks ago literally
on the side of the road.

00:12:41.970 --> 00:12:44.237
Now i run into her in
some random chicago bar --

00:12:44.270 --> 00:12:45.771
The same bar where a waitress

00:12:45.804 --> 00:12:47.838
Was slaughtered by
something supernatural.

00:12:47.870 --> 00:12:49.804
You don't think that's
weird? It happens.

00:12:49.838 --> 00:12:51.870
Well, yeah, it happens, but not to us.

00:12:51.903 --> 00:12:53.104
Look, i could be wrong.

00:12:53.137 --> 00:12:55.471
I'm just saying there's
something about this girl

00:12:55.504 --> 00:12:57.137
That i can't quite put my finger on.

00:12:57.170 --> 00:12:58.804
But i bet you'd like to.

00:12:58.838 --> 00:13:00.504
But maybe she's not a suspect.

00:13:00.537 --> 00:13:02.437
Maybe you got a thing for her, huh?

00:13:02.471 --> 00:13:05.771
You're thinking too much
with your upstairs brain, huh?

00:13:05.804 --> 00:13:07.838
Do me a favor.

00:13:07.870 --> 00:13:11.037
Check and see if there's a
meg masters from massachusetts

00:13:11.070 --> 00:13:13.504
And see if you can't dig
anything up on that symbol.

00:13:13.537 --> 00:13:14.970
What are you gonna do?

00:13:15.003 --> 00:13:16.771
I'm gonna watch meg.

00:13:16.804 --> 00:13:18.204
Yeah.

00:13:18.237 --> 00:13:19.771
I just want to see what's what.

00:13:19.804 --> 00:13:21.304
All right, you little pervert.

00:13:21.337 --> 00:13:23.337
I'm going. I'm going.

00:13:47.504 --> 00:13:48.804
Hey.

00:13:48.838 --> 00:13:50.704
You're lurking outside
that poor girl's apartment,

00:13:50.738 --> 00:13:52.504
Aren't you? No.

00:13:54.037 --> 00:13:55.838
Yes.

00:13:55.870 --> 00:13:57.970
You've got a funny way
of showing your affection.

00:13:58.003 --> 00:14:00.671
You find anything on her or what?

00:14:00.704 --> 00:14:02.671
There's a meg masters in
the andover phone book.

00:14:02.704 --> 00:14:04.704
I even pulled up her high-School photo.

00:14:04.738 --> 00:14:06.870
Now, look, why don't
you go knock on her door

00:14:06.903 --> 00:14:09.204
And invite her to a poetry reading

00:14:09.237 --> 00:14:11.704
Or whatever it is you do, huh?

00:14:11.738 --> 00:14:13.771
What about the symbol? Any luck?

00:14:13.804 --> 00:14:16.070
Yeah, that i did have some luck with.

00:14:16.104 --> 00:14:20.070
Turns out it's zoroastrian.

00:14:20.104 --> 00:14:22.937
Very, very old-School, like
2,000 years before christ.

00:14:22.970 --> 00:14:24.437
It's a sigil for a daeva.

00:14:24.471 --> 00:14:25.903
What's a daeva?

00:14:25.937 --> 00:14:27.903
It translates to
"demon of darkness" --

00:14:27.937 --> 00:14:30.237
Zoroastrian demons, and
they're savage, animalistic,

00:14:30.270 --> 00:14:34.070
Nasty attitudes -- Kind
of like demonic pit bulls.

00:14:34.104 --> 00:14:36.270
How did you figure that out?

00:14:36.304 --> 00:14:38.404
You don't have a corner on
paper chasing around here.

00:14:38.437 --> 00:14:39.870
Name the last book you read.

00:14:41.903 --> 00:14:44.371
I called dad's friend
caleb. He told me, all right.

00:14:44.404 --> 00:14:45.804
Anyway, here's the thing.

00:14:45.838 --> 00:14:48.070
These daevas, they have to be summoned.

00:14:48.104 --> 00:14:49.771
So someone's controlling it?

00:14:49.804 --> 00:14:51.270
Yeah, that's what i'm saying.

00:14:51.304 --> 00:14:53.804
And from what i gather, it's
pretty risky business, too.

00:14:53.838 --> 00:14:56.237
These suckers tend to bite
the hand that feeds them...

00:14:56.270 --> 00:14:58.771
And the arms and the torsos.

00:14:58.804 --> 00:14:59.970
What do they look like?

00:15:00.003 --> 00:15:02.137
Nobody's seen them for
a couple of millennia.

00:15:02.170 --> 00:15:03.771
Summoning a demon that ancient,

00:15:03.804 --> 00:15:05.504
Someone really knows their stuff.

00:15:05.537 --> 00:15:07.371
I think we've got a
major player in town.

00:15:08.838 --> 00:15:11.471
Why don't you go give that
girl a private strip-O-Gram?

00:15:11.504 --> 00:15:13.270
<i>Bite me. Bite her.</i>

00:15:13.304 --> 00:15:15.170
Don't leave teeth marks, though.

00:15:15.204 --> 00:15:17.170
Sam? Are
you --

00:15:46.337 --> 00:15:47.704
No, no,
i'm just --

00:15:47.738 --> 00:15:49.604
Pervert!

00:15:49.637 --> 00:15:52.237
What a creep!

00:18:46.270 --> 00:18:48.571
I don't think you should come

00:18:48.604 --> 00:18:51.404
Because the brothers
-- They're in town.

00:18:51.437 --> 00:18:53.104
I didn't
know that --

00:18:58.237 --> 00:18:59.537
Yes, sir.

00:18:59.571 --> 00:19:05.037
Yes, i'll be here... waiting for you.

00:20:29.337 --> 00:20:32.471
What the hell?

00:20:37.971 --> 00:20:40.603
Dude, i've got to talk to you.

00:20:40.637 --> 00:20:42.804
So, hot little meg is
summoning the daeva?

00:20:42.837 --> 00:20:45.071
It looks like she was
using that black altar

00:20:45.104 --> 00:20:46.404
To control the thing.

00:20:46.438 --> 00:20:48.737
So sammy's got a thing for the bad girl.

00:20:48.770 --> 00:20:50.704
And what's the deal
with that bowl again?

00:20:50.737 --> 00:20:52.537
She was talking
into it --

00:20:52.570 --> 00:20:54.670
The way witches used to
scry into crystal balls.

00:20:54.704 --> 00:20:56.304
She was communicating with someone.

00:20:56.338 --> 00:20:58.971
With the daeva? No, you said
those things were savages.

00:20:59.004 --> 00:21:01.271
No, this was someone different,

00:21:01.304 --> 00:21:03.603
Someone who's giving her orders,

00:21:03.637 --> 00:21:06.371
Someone who's coming to that warehouse.

00:21:15.371 --> 00:21:16.503
Holy crap.

00:21:16.537 --> 00:21:17.971
What?

00:21:18.004 --> 00:21:19.971
What i was gonna tell you earlier.

00:21:20.004 --> 00:21:22.470
I pulled a favor with my

00:21:22.503 --> 00:21:24.937
Friend amy over at
the police department.

00:21:24.971 --> 00:21:27.503
Complete records of the two victims.

00:21:27.537 --> 00:21:29.237
We missed something the first time.

00:21:29.271 --> 00:21:31.904
What?

00:21:31.937 --> 00:21:35.438
The first victim
-- The old man?

00:21:35.470 --> 00:21:37.804
He spent his whole life in chicago,

00:21:37.837 --> 00:21:40.570
But look where he was
born. Lawrence, kansas.

00:21:40.603 --> 00:21:41.904
Mm-Hmm.

00:21:41.937 --> 00:21:43.804
Meredith -- The
second victim?

00:21:43.837 --> 00:21:45.637
It turns out she was adopted.

00:21:45.670 --> 00:21:47.470
And guess where she's from?

00:21:54.837 --> 00:21:55.971
Holy crap.

00:21:56.004 --> 00:21:57.304
Yeah.

00:21:57.338 --> 00:21:59.570
I mean, that is where
the demon killed mom.

00:22:01.304 --> 00:22:02.971
You think meg's tied up with the demon?

00:22:03.004 --> 00:22:05.438
I think it's a definite possibility.

00:22:05.470 --> 00:22:07.971
What's the significance of lawrence?

00:22:08.004 --> 00:22:09.637
And how do these daeva things fit in?

00:22:09.670 --> 00:22:11.971
I say we trash that
black altar, grab meg,

00:22:12.004 --> 00:22:14.737
And have ourselves a
friendly little interrogation.

00:22:14.770 --> 00:22:16.603
No, we can't. We shouldn't tip her off.

00:22:16.637 --> 00:22:18.737
We've got to stake out that warehouse.

00:22:18.770 --> 00:22:21.570
We've got to see who...or
what is showing up to meet her.

00:22:21.603 --> 00:22:22.904
I'll tell you one thing.

00:22:22.937 --> 00:22:25.603
I don't think we should do this alone.

00:22:28.004 --> 00:22:29.470
We think we've got a serious lead

00:22:29.503 --> 00:22:31.137
On the thing that killed mom.

00:22:31.171 --> 00:22:37.304
So, uh, this warehouse
-- It's 1435 west erie.

00:22:37.338 --> 00:22:38.971
Dad, if you get this,

00:22:39.004 --> 00:22:41.837
Get to chicago as soon as you can.

00:22:41.870 --> 00:22:43.503
Voice mail?

00:22:43.537 --> 00:22:44.837
Yeah.

00:22:46.037 --> 00:22:47.503
Jeez. What'd you get?

00:22:47.537 --> 00:22:50.603
I ransacked
that trunk --

00:22:50.637 --> 00:22:53.104
Holy water, y weapon
that i could think of.

00:22:53.137 --> 00:22:56.537
Exorcism rituals from about
a half-Dozen religions.

00:22:56.570 --> 00:22:59.637
I'm not sure what to expect,

00:22:59.670 --> 00:23:02.603
So i guess we should just
expect everything, huh?

00:23:10.704 --> 00:23:13.338
It's a big night.

00:23:13.371 --> 00:23:15.937
Yeah.

00:23:15.971 --> 00:23:17.237
You nervous?

00:23:17.271 --> 00:23:20.770
No. No, are you?

00:23:20.804 --> 00:23:22.971
No. No way.

00:23:31.371 --> 00:23:33.171
God, could you imagine if we actually

00:23:33.204 --> 00:23:34.870
Found that damn thing, that demon?

00:23:34.904 --> 00:23:36.971
Let's not get ahead of
ourselves, all right?

00:23:37.004 --> 00:23:41.770
I know. I'm just
saying... what if we did?

00:23:41.804 --> 00:23:44.804
What if this whole
thing was over tonight?

00:23:44.837 --> 00:23:46.971
Man, i'd sleep for a month,

00:23:47.004 --> 00:23:50.837
Go back to school,
just be a person again.

00:23:50.870 --> 00:23:52.904
You want to go back to school?

00:23:52.937 --> 00:23:55.537
Yeah, once we're done hunting the thing.

00:23:56.704 --> 00:23:59.271
Why? Is there something wrong with that?

00:23:59.304 --> 00:24:03.037
No, no, it's great. Good for you.

00:24:03.071 --> 00:24:06.637
I mean, what are you gonna
do when it's all over?

00:24:06.670 --> 00:24:08.770
It's never gonna be over.

00:24:08.804 --> 00:24:10.071
There's gonna be others.

00:24:10.104 --> 00:24:12.371
There's always gonna
be something to hunt.

00:24:12.404 --> 00:24:15.204
But there's got to be something
that you want for yourself.

00:24:15.237 --> 00:24:17.637
I don't want you to leave
the second this is over.

00:24:17.670 --> 00:24:21.537
Dude, what's your problem?

00:24:27.503 --> 00:24:30.503
Why do you think i drag
you everywhere, huh?

00:24:30.537 --> 00:24:33.737
Why do you think i came
and got you at stanford?

00:24:33.770 --> 00:24:36.004
'Cause dad was in trouble.

00:24:36.037 --> 00:24:38.670
'Cause you wanted to find
the thing that killed mom.

00:24:38.704 --> 00:24:40.837
Yes, that, but it's more than that, man.

00:24:47.371 --> 00:24:52.004
You and me
and dad --

00:24:52.037 --> 00:24:55.404
I want us to be together again.

00:24:57.371 --> 00:25:01.670
I want us to be a family again.

00:25:01.704 --> 00:25:06.371
<i>Dean, we are a family.
I'd do anything for you.</i>

00:25:06.404 --> 00:25:09.404
But things will never be
the way they were before.

00:25:15.004 --> 00:25:17.670
They could be.

00:25:21.371 --> 00:25:23.037
I don't want them to be.

00:25:27.204 --> 00:25:29.204
I'm not gonna live this life forever.

00:25:29.237 --> 00:25:32.570
Dean, when this is all over,

00:25:32.603 --> 00:25:35.837
You're gonna have to
let me go my own way.

00:26:38.603 --> 00:26:42.870
Guys. Hiding is a little bit
childish, don't you think?

00:26:42.904 --> 00:26:44.870
That didn't work out like i'd planned.

00:26:47.804 --> 00:26:47.904
Why don't you come out?

00:26:58.071 --> 00:27:01.570
Sam, i have to say,

00:27:01.603 --> 00:27:04.304
This puts a real crimp
in our relationship.

00:27:04.338 --> 00:27:06.171
Yeah, tell me about it.

00:27:06.204 --> 00:27:08.870
So, where's your little daeva friend?

00:27:08.904 --> 00:27:10.104
Around.

00:27:10.137 --> 00:27:12.770
And that shotgun's
not gonna do much good.

00:27:12.804 --> 00:27:14.704
Oh, don't worry, sweetheart.

00:27:14.737 --> 00:27:16.237
The shotgun's not for the demon.

00:27:16.271 --> 00:27:19.837
So, who is it, meg? Who's coming?

00:27:19.870 --> 00:27:21.338
Who are you waiting for?

00:27:21.371 --> 00:27:23.870
You.

00:27:54.121 --> 00:27:57.287
Hey, sam, don't take this the wrong way,

00:27:57.321 --> 00:28:00.653
But your girlfriend... is a bitch.

00:28:00.687 --> 00:28:04.854
This, the whole thing, was a trap.

00:28:06.753 --> 00:28:09.387
Running into you at the bar,

00:28:09.421 --> 00:28:13.121
Following you here, hearing
what you had to say --

00:28:13.154 --> 00:28:15.187
It was all a setup, wasn't it?

00:28:16.787 --> 00:28:18.787
And that the victims were from lawrence.

00:28:18.820 --> 00:28:20.187
It doesn't mean anything.

00:28:20.221 --> 00:28:22.820
It was just to draw you in, that's all.

00:28:22.854 --> 00:28:24.687
You killed those two people for nothing.

00:28:24.720 --> 00:28:26.987
Baby, i've killed a
lot more for a lot less.

00:28:28.887 --> 00:28:32.020
You trapped us. Good for you.

00:28:32.054 --> 00:28:34.354
It's miller time.

00:28:34.387 --> 00:28:36.187
Why don't you kill us already?

00:28:36.221 --> 00:28:39.321
Not very quick on the uptake, are we?

00:28:44.954 --> 00:28:46.620
This trap isn't for you.

00:28:50.488 --> 00:28:51.653
Dad.

00:28:52.820 --> 00:28:54.254
It's a trap for dad.

00:28:57.121 --> 00:28:59.954
Oh, sweetheart, you're
dumber than you look.

00:28:59.987 --> 00:29:03.920
'Cause even if dad was
in town, which he is not,

00:29:03.954 --> 00:29:05.920
He wouldn't walk into
something like this.

00:29:05.954 --> 00:29:07.653
He's too good.

00:29:07.687 --> 00:29:10.020
He is pretty good, i'll give you that.

00:29:15.020 --> 00:29:17.020
But you see

00:29:22.354 --> 00:29:24.154
He has one weakness.

00:29:24.187 --> 00:29:25.521
What's that?

00:29:25.554 --> 00:29:27.287
You.

00:29:28.687 --> 00:29:31.554
He lets his guard down around his boys,

00:29:31.588 --> 00:29:34.954
Lets his emotions cloud his judgment.

00:29:36.920 --> 00:29:39.720
<i>I happen to know he is in town,</i>

00:29:39.753 --> 00:29:44.488
And he'll come and try to save you.

00:29:44.521 --> 00:29:47.387
And then the daevas
will kill everybody --

00:29:47.421 --> 00:29:51.987
Nice and slow... and messy.

00:29:52.020 --> 00:29:54.321
Well, i've got news for you.

00:29:54.354 --> 00:29:57.653
It's gonna take a lot more
than some...shadow to kill him.

00:29:57.687 --> 00:29:59.854
Oh, the daevas are in the room here.

00:29:59.887 --> 00:30:01.087
They're invisible.

00:30:01.121 --> 00:30:03.454
Their shadows are just
the only part you can see.

00:30:03.488 --> 00:30:04.987
Why are you doing this, meg?

00:30:05.020 --> 00:30:07.221
What kind of deal you got
worked out here, huh...

00:30:07.254 --> 00:30:08.554
And with who?

00:30:08.588 --> 00:30:10.488
I'm doing this for the same reasons

00:30:10.521 --> 00:30:12.488
You do what
you do --

00:30:12.521 --> 00:30:14.854
Loyalty, love.

00:30:20.521 --> 00:30:22.488
Like the love you had for
mommy...and jess.Go to he

00:30:22.521 --> 00:30:26.054
Baby, i'm already there.

00:30:28.087 --> 00:30:30.221
Come on, sam.

00:30:30.254 --> 00:30:33.254
There's no need to be nasty.

00:30:37.753 --> 00:30:41.720
I think we both know...

00:30:41.753 --> 00:30:44.588
How you really feel about me.

00:30:48.020 --> 00:30:49.687
You know

00:30:51.753 --> 00:30:55.720
I saw you... watching me...

00:30:55.753 --> 00:30:59.287
Changing in my apartment.

00:30:59.321 --> 00:31:01.887
It turned you on, didn't it?

00:31:01.920 --> 00:31:03.920
Get a room, you two.

00:31:03.954 --> 00:31:05.454
I didn't mind.

00:31:05.488 --> 00:31:08.121
I liked that you were watching me.

00:31:08.154 --> 00:31:10.121
Come on, sammy,

00:31:10.154 --> 00:31:13.121
You and i can still
have a little dirty fun.

00:31:13.154 --> 00:31:15.753
You want to have fun? Go ahead, then.

00:31:15.787 --> 00:31:18.287
I'm a little tied up right now.

00:31:53.488 --> 00:31:56.454
Now, were you just trying to distract me

00:31:56.488 --> 00:31:59.620
While your brother cuts free?

00:31:59.653 --> 00:32:02.287
No.

00:32:02.321 --> 00:32:04.287
No.

00:32:04.321 --> 00:32:07.187
It was because i have a knife of my own.

00:32:09.887 --> 00:32:11.187
Sam!

00:32:11.221 --> 00:32:13.054
Get the altar.

00:32:52.720 --> 00:32:54.354
So, i guess the daevas

00:32:54.388 --> 00:32:56.687
Didn't like being bossed around.

00:32:56.720 --> 00:32:58.854
I guess not.

00:32:58.887 --> 00:33:00.187
Hey, sam?

00:33:00.221 --> 00:33:01.354
Hmm?

00:33:01.388 --> 00:33:03.354
Next time you want to get laid,

00:33:03.388 --> 00:33:07.054
Find a girl that's not
so buckets of crazy, huh?

00:33:21.854 --> 00:33:24.254
Why don't you just leave
that stuff in the car?

00:33:24.288 --> 00:33:26.587
I said it before, and
i'll say it again --

00:33:26.620 --> 00:33:29.787
Better safe than sorry.

00:33:33.354 --> 00:33:34.520
Hey!

00:33:47.420 --> 00:33:49.021
Dad.

00:33:49.054 --> 00:33:51.054
Hey, boys.

00:34:19.420 --> 00:34:20.553
Hi, sam.

00:34:20.587 --> 00:34:21.921
Hi, dad.

00:34:25.453 --> 00:34:27.754
Dad, it was a trap.

00:34:27.787 --> 00:34:31.420
I didn't know. I'm sorry.

00:34:31.453 --> 00:34:34.553
It's all right. I thought
it might have been.

00:34:34.587 --> 00:34:36.121
Were you there?

00:34:36.154 --> 00:34:40.487
I got there just in time to
see the girl take the swan dive.

00:34:40.520 --> 00:34:41.887
She was the bad guy, right?

00:34:41.921 --> 00:34:43.420
Yes, sir.Yes, sir.

00:34:43.453 --> 00:34:45.921
Good. Well, it doesn't surprise me.

00:34:45.954 --> 00:34:48.388
It's tried to stop me before.

00:34:48.453 --> 00:34:50.420
The demon has?

00:34:50.453 --> 00:34:53.754
It knows i'm close. It
knows i'm gonna kill it.

00:34:53.787 --> 00:34:57.354
Not just exorcise it
or send it back to hell,

00:34:57.388 --> 00:35:00.154
Actually kill it.

00:35:00.187 --> 00:35:01.754
How?

00:35:01.787 --> 00:35:04.854
I'm working on that.

00:35:04.887 --> 00:35:08.520
Let us come with you. We'll help.

00:35:08.553 --> 00:35:12.121
No, sam.

00:35:12.154 --> 00:35:13.187
Not yet.

00:35:13.221 --> 00:35:15.453
Listen, try to understand.

00:35:15.487 --> 00:35:17.921
This demon is a scary son of a bitch.

00:35:17.954 --> 00:35:20.587
I don't want you
caught in the crossfire.

00:35:20.620 --> 00:35:21.921
I don't want you hurt.

00:35:21.954 --> 00:35:24.087
You don't have to worry about us.

00:35:24.121 --> 00:35:25.121
Of course i do.

00:35:27.453 --> 00:35:29.453
I'm your father.

00:35:33.487 --> 00:35:37.787
Listen, sammy, the last
time we were together,

00:35:37.820 --> 00:35:39.620
We had one hell of a fight.

00:35:39.654 --> 00:35:40.787
Yes, sir.

00:35:48.654 --> 00:35:51.620
It's good to see you again.

00:35:51.654 --> 00:35:53.487
It's been a long time.

00:35:55.887 --> 00:35:57.221
Too long.

00:36:24.720 --> 00:36:26.221
No!

00:37:04.967 --> 00:37:06.834
These things are shadow demons,

00:37:06.867 --> 00:37:08.567
So let's light 'em up!

00:37:23.533 --> 00:37:24.667
Dad!

00:37:24.700 --> 00:37:25.901
Over here!

00:37:28.101 --> 00:37:30.334
Come on!

00:37:55.167 --> 00:37:57.467
All right, come on. We
don't have much time.

00:37:57.500 --> 00:37:59.967
As soon as the flare's
out, they'll be back.

00:38:00.001 --> 00:38:01.533
Wait, wait!

00:38:01.567 --> 00:38:03.934
Sam, wait.

00:38:07.567 --> 00:38:09.034
Dad, you can't come with us.

00:38:09.067 --> 00:38:14.268
What? What are you talking about?

00:38:14.301 --> 00:38:15.800
We'll be all right.

00:38:15.834 --> 00:38:18.600
Dean, we should stick together!
We'll go after those --

00:38:18.634 --> 00:38:19.967
Sam, listen to me!

00:38:22.901 --> 00:38:24.934
We almost got dad killed in there.

00:38:24.967 --> 00:38:27.934
Don't you understand?
They're not gonna stop.

00:38:27.967 --> 00:38:29.533
They're gonna try again.

00:38:29.567 --> 00:38:31.967
They're gonna use us to get to him.

00:38:32.001 --> 00:38:33.667
I mean, meg was right.

00:38:33.700 --> 00:38:36.500
Dad's vulnerable when he's with us.

00:38:38.101 --> 00:38:42.500
He...he's stronger without us around.

00:38:44.567 --> 00:38:46.234
Dad...

00:38:47.934 --> 00:38:49.901
No.

00:38:49.934 --> 00:38:52.034
After everything,

00:38:52.067 --> 00:38:54.800
After all the time we
spent looking for you,

00:38:54.834 --> 00:38:57.334
Please.

00:38:57.368 --> 00:38:59.101
I've got to be a part of this fight.

00:38:59.134 --> 00:39:01.101
Sammy, this fight is just starting,

00:39:01.134 --> 00:39:03.834
And we are all gonna
have a part to play.

00:39:03.867 --> 00:39:05.600
For now, you've got to trust me, son.

00:39:07.967 --> 00:39:11.901
Okay? You've got to let me go.

00:39:55.734 --> 00:39:57.867
Be careful, boys.

00:39:59.167 --> 00:40:01.001
Come on.



00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:04.000
